@node "Brief Description"

Brief Description:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	If you`re running a BBS on /X, you surely know that problem:
	somebody pumps up tons of warez, just before he`s finished,
	the BBS crashes and after the reboot, all those files are
	flying around in nodeX/playpen, it`s not possible to resume them
	or enter a description, until the sysop moves `em to the right
	directories. This is, where ©PPTPUM comes in: it will scan all
	your playpen dirs for files, if something is found, it will scan
	the @{"callerslog" link "Configuration, installation, etc..."} of the correspondig node for the uploader and
	the right conference and then move the files to the according
	directories, ready for the user to resume.
	Now, why use this one ? There are already tools out, that do
	the same ? Correct, but this one is by far the best, just read
	on, and you`ll know why !


@endnode

@node "Configuration, installation, etc..."

Configuration, installation, etc...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	First, you will have to do some configuration stuff. Just use
	your favourite txt-editor ( ©Cygnus Ed, ©Edge, ©EdWard, ... )
	and create a file like this:

s:lep-np.cfg
bbs:bbs/NewUsers/partupload/
bbs:bbs/PublicDomain/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Amiga/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Sysops/partupload/
bbs:bbs/PC/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Requests/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Ae-Support/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Pics/partupload/
bbs:bbs/Coders/partupload/

	The first line has to be a path & filename of your choice, it`s
	where ©PPTPUM will look for your node-config file, we`ll talk
	about that later on.
	The other lines are simply the full paths to each conference`s
	partupload-directory. Be sure, you put them in the right order,
	means, conference 1 first, then conference 2, ...up to conference 9.
	Don`t forget the `/` at the end of each path !
	Now save this file to wherever you like, this will be the main-
	config file.

	Now, you have to create another file, with information about
	your nodes in it, this should look like that:

bbs:bbs/node0/playpen/
bbs:bbs/node0/callerslog
bbs:bbs/node1/playpen/
bbs:bbs/node1/callerslog
bbs:bbs/node2/playpen/
bbs:bbs/node2/callerslog

	This would be an example for a BBS with 3 nodes.
	Line 1 is the path of the node`s playpen dir, line 2 is the
	path & name of the callerslog for that node, just do that for
	all nodes you have, and you`re done. Save this, just as you wrote
	in the first line of the main-config, e.g. in this example as
	`s:lep-np.cfg`.

	Now just put ©PPTPUM in your startup-sequence, with the path &
	name of the main-config as an argument, e.g. PPTPUMV1.5 s:LEP-PPM.cfg
	DO NOT put any comment in at the end of this line, the path 
	HAS to end with a RETURN, there`s no real argument-parsing !


	That`s it for the normal stuff, ©PPTPUM will do it`s work now...
	....BUT: have you ever seen something like that in your
	callerslog ??

**************************************************************
02-04-94 (13:56:22) [113] MORGOTH (CONNECT 14400/ARQ/V42b) -HADES-
	Resuming cls_ff1.dms  614878 bytes [219136]
	Uploading ipt-cka.nfo  4934 bytes
	Uploading ipt-cka1.dms 469983 bytes
	Uploading ipt-cka2.dms 582783 bytes
	Uploading ipt-cka3.dms 562510 bytes
	Uploading ipt-cka4.dms 559318 bytes
	Uploading sr-elan2.dms 390395 bytes


	As you can see, there`s no information about the conference, in
	which the upload took place in this callerslog-entry !
	This happens, whenever a user is resuming an upload after a
	loss carrier. Now, there would be no possibility to move the
	files to the correct directory for any available playpen-mover !
	But ©PPTPUM offers you another chance in such cases, it is able
	to move files according to their extensions (.DMS, .ZIP, ...) !
	For instance, you have an AMIGA-conf & a PC-conf: now, DMS or LHA
	files will surely belong to the AMIGA-conf, ZIP, ARJ belongs most
	likely to the PC-section. So you can tell ©PPTPUM, to move these
	files to the right conferences ! To do so, you have to create
	another file, which has to be called `Lep-PPDF.cfg` and has to
	reside in s:
	©PPTPUM will look for this file, if it`s found, extension-moving
	will be on, else off. This file has to look like that:

.arj5.zip5.dms2.txt6.ARJ5.ZIP5.DMS2.TXT6.lha2.LHA2

	This means: ARJ and ZIP will go to conf 5, TXT will go to conf 6
	DMS and LHA will be moved to conf 2 ! You can do this for any
	extension & conference you like, just add it to `Lep-PPDF.cfg` !
	Each entry must consist of the extension followed by the conference
	to move to, e.g. `.ZOM4`, do this in lower- and uppercase !
	Just put all these entries in ONE line, with a RETURN at the end
	of the line. Up to 20 extensions are supported !
	Now, ©PPTPUM will do it`s normal work, and in case, it can`t find
	information on the correct conference, it will look for the
	extensions and only if even this fails, the file will stay in
	playpen !

@endnode

@node Limitations

Limitations:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
	- Up to 10 nodes are supported
	- Up to 10 conferences are supported
	- Up to 20 extensions can be used

	If there is a demand, i can extend those limitations of coz !

@endnode

